   "id": "nvidia-ceo-exit",
   "group": "Tech & AI",
   "headline": "Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns; CFO Colette Kress steps in as interim chief",
   "when": "Wed 11 Nov board vote · filed Thu 12 Nov",
   "what": "Nvidia told the SEC that its board accepted Huang’s resignation as CEO and director, effective immediately. Kress, the CFO since 2013, is interim CEO while keeping her finance role, and Harvey Jones is the new board chair. Nvidia shares fell about 2% on Friday after dropping more than 4% on Thursday. The Nasdaq-100 closed down 1.2% on Friday.",
   "why": "You hold Nvidia directly only at 0.2%, but it is a heavy weight in the S&P 500 funds (ES-US500RMF, K-USA-A(D)) and in your semiconductor and AI funds. Analysts quoted by CNBC say Nvidia may find it harder to arrange big new financing deals for AI partners. Nvidia reports results on Tue 17 Nov.",
